Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• Subjects.CategoryID ­– identify English courses (CategoryID = 'ENG').  
• Subjects.SubjectID – join to Classes.SubjectID.  
• Classes.SubjectID – attach every class to its discipline.  
• Classes.ClassID – join to Student_Schedules.ClassID.  
• Student_Schedules.ClassID – points to the class the student took.  
• Student_Schedules.StudentID – join to Students.StudentID.  
• Student_Schedules.ClassStatus – keep only completions (ClassStatus = 2).  
• Student_Schedules.Grade – numeric grade used for ranking / quintiles.  
• Students.StudLastName – the last name we need to list.  

Typical conditions  

• Subjects.CategoryID = 'ENG' (English)  
• Student_Schedules.ClassStatus = 2            -- completed  
• Student_Schedules.Grade IS NOT NULL          -- make sure there is a grade  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑complex SELECT statements (each different) that progressively reveal the needed data and finally produce the requested quintile list.  All queries are limited to 20 rows so they can be run safely for inspection.

```sql
-- 1) Look at all subject categories to confirm the ENG code
SELECT DISTINCT "CategoryID"
FROM "Subjects"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Show a few English subjects
SELECT DISTINCT "SubjectID",
       "SubjectCode",
       "SubjectName"
FROM "Subjects"
WHERE "CategoryID" = 'ENG'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Which classes are tied to English subjects?
SELECT DISTINCT c."ClassID",
       c."SubjectID"
FROM "Classes" AS c
JOIN "Subjects" AS s
     ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
WHERE s."CategoryID" = 'ENG'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Peek at student schedules that reference ENG classes
SELECT DISTINCT ss."StudentID",
       ss."ClassID",
       ss."ClassStatus",
       ss."Grade"
FROM "Student_Schedules" AS ss
JOIN "Classes" AS c
     ON c."ClassID" = ss."ClassID"
JOIN "Subjects" AS s
     ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
WHERE s."CategoryID" = 'ENG'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Restrict to completed English courses (ClassStatus = 2)
SELECT DISTINCT ss."StudentID",
       ss."ClassID",
       ss."Grade"
FROM "Student_Schedules" AS ss
JOIN "Classes"        AS c  ON c."ClassID"   = ss."ClassID"
JOIN "Subjects"       AS s  ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
WHERE s."CategoryID"  = 'ENG'
  AND ss."ClassStatus" = 2
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Bring in student names
SELECT DISTINCT st."StudLastName",
       ss."Grade"
FROM "Student_Schedules" AS ss
JOIN "Classes"  AS c  ON c."ClassID"   = ss."ClassID"
JOIN "Subjects" AS s  ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
JOIN "Students" AS st ON st."StudentID"= ss."StudentID"
WHERE s."CategoryID" = 'ENG'
  AND ss."ClassStatus" = 2
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) How many completions exist?  (total N will drive quintiles)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "Total_Completed_ENG_Grades"
FROM "Student_Schedules" AS ss
JOIN "Classes"  AS c  ON c."ClassID"   = ss."ClassID"
JOIN "Subjects" AS s  ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
WHERE s."CategoryID" = 'ENG'
  AND ss."ClassStatus" = 2;
```

```sql
-- 8) Add a descending rank for each grade
SELECT st."StudLastName",
       ss."Grade",
       DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY ss."Grade" DESC) AS "Rank"
FROM "Student_Schedules" AS ss
JOIN "Classes"  AS c  ON c."ClassID"   = ss."ClassID"
JOIN "Subjects" AS s  ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
JOIN "Students" AS st ON st."StudentID"= ss."StudentID"
WHERE s."CategoryID" = 'ENG'
  AND ss."ClassStatus" = 2
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Compute percentile position (rank / total) and label quintile
SELECT *
FROM (
       SELECT st."StudLastName",
              ss."Grade",
              DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY ss."Grade" DESC)                           AS "Rank",
              COUNT(*)   OVER ()                                                    AS "Total",
              (1.0 * DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY ss."Grade" DESC))
              / COUNT(*) OVER ()                                                    AS "Pct"
       FROM "Student_Schedules" AS ss
       JOIN "Classes"  AS c  ON c."ClassID"   = ss."ClassID"
       JOIN "Subjects" AS s  ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
       JOIN "Students" AS st ON st."StudentID"= ss."StudentID"
       WHERE s."CategoryID" = 'ENG'
         AND ss."ClassStatus" = 2
) AS x
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL ANSWER → last names with quintile labels, sorted First–Fifth
SELECT "StudLastName",
       CASE
            WHEN "Pct" <= 0.20 THEN 'First'
            WHEN "Pct" <= 0.40 THEN 'Second'
            WHEN "Pct" <= 0.60 THEN 'Third'
            WHEN "Pct" <= 0.80 THEN 'Fourth'
            ELSE                        'Fifth'
       END AS "Quintile"
FROM (
       SELECT st."StudLastName",
              DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY ss."Grade" DESC) * 1.0
              / COUNT(*) OVER ()                                       AS "Pct"
       FROM "Student_Schedules" AS ss
       JOIN "Classes"  AS c  ON c."ClassID"   = ss."ClassID"
       JOIN "Subjects" AS s  ON s."SubjectID" = c."SubjectID"
       JOIN "Students" AS st ON st."StudentID"= ss."StudentID"
       WHERE s."CategoryID" = 'ENG'
         AND ss."ClassStatus" = 2
) AS ranked
ORDER BY
     CASE
          WHEN "Quintile" = 'First'  THEN 1
          WHEN "Quintile" = 'Second' THEN 2
          WHEN "Quintile" = 'Third'  THEN 3
          WHEN "Quintile" = 'Fourth' THEN 4
          ELSE                           5
     END,
     "StudLastName"
LIMIT 20;
```
Each query can be run in sequence to explore the data all the way to the requested quintile report.
